  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/265043450",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/1801#issuecomment-265043450",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/1801",
    "id": 265043450,
    "node_id": "MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2NTA0MzQ1MA==",
    "user": {
      "login": "kojiishi",
      "id": 1274377,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzQzNzc=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1274377?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/kojiishi",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/kojiishi",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kojiishi/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kojiishi/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kojiishi/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kojiishi/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kojiishi/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kojiishi/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kojiishi/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kojiishi/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kojiishi/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "created_at": "2016-12-06T02:32:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-12-06T02:32:39Z",
    "body": ">> I think for CJK languages, majority of people would prefer either fullwidth parentheses or proportional parentheses with whitespace around. Maybe proportional parentheses are more desirable for other languages? Although it seems to me CJK languages (especially Japanese) are the main user of ruby.\r\n\r\n> That’s note quite true. People DO use proportional (half-width) parenthesis in Japanese without spaces. I’ve rarely seen anyone inserting spaces around parenthesis in Japanese for that matter.\r\n\r\nI agree, but since we have to choose one, I think you'll find \"typically\" if you look at referring bugs and discussion at I18N WG, and I agree with I18N that if we pick typically used one, that'd be fullwidth.\r\n\r\nThe larger issue than width is the baseline. ASCII parentheses are usually designed to match to x-height, which is too low to use for CJK, while fullwidth parentheses are designed to match to em-height. There are a few fonts that has em-height parentheses for ASCII parentheses but they're really a few, I know only 3, because doing so sacrifices English rendering.\r\n\r\nIn today's fonts environment, if we want parentheses that matches to CJK without extra spacing, we need to use fullwidth code points with `pwid` OpenType feature.\r\n\r\n> Inserting parenthesis is quite important for copy & paste...\r\n\r\nI'll leave @tkent-google on whether we want to do this or not.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/265043450/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
      "+1": 0,
      "-1": 0,
      "laugh": 0,
      "hooray": 0,
      "confused": 0,
      "heart": 0,
      "rocket": 0,
      "eyes": 0
    },
